[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3 uid="uid://c8primm001"]

; PRIMM, SKINNED — bead godot-test1-5u3.6, the second hero in this game on a
; Skeleton3D and the first one whose HEAD BONE does any work. One mesh on MPFB2's
; `game_engine` rig, 23 bones after `build_hero.cut_fingers()`, built by
; `scripts/build_hero.py --hero primm` (the source of record;
; `assets/models/characters/PROVENANCE.md` carries the row). The ten parts this
; scene used to instance — nine generated and one authored head — and the
; generator that wrote them are retired with this bead: the face is the SAME
; z3e.12 recipe, built into this .glb from a `build_hero.FACES` row rather than
; exported separately and hung on a neck.
;
; THE SCENE IS THE FLAG, exactly as `teibi.tscn` says: the Skeleton3D under `Body`
; is what makes `hero_rig.gd` hand him to `hero_rig_skeleton.gd` (bd 5u3.2), so
; `player_animation.gd`, `remote_avatar.gd`, `player_controller.gd` and
; `player_abilities.gd` change by zero lines for this migration.
;
; AND PRIMM IS WHAT FIRST MOVES THE HEAD BONE. `GAITS.primm` asks for `head_deg`
; 3 and he is the first SHIPPED hero on this rig to do so — Teibi's row asks for
; none, so until now the skinned `head_bobble()` write was exercised only by
; `gait_selfcheck` check 8's fixture, which forces it on. From this scene onward
; check 2's "expression" assertion measures it on the live hero through
; `rig.measure().head_z`, and deleting the write turns that check red.
;
; THE UID IS LOAD-BEARING and stays `uid://c8primm001`: `player_controller.gd`'s
; CHARACTERS points at the PATH, but a changed uid makes Godot rewrite every
; reference that resolved this scene by uid, and warn while it does it.
;
; `Body` stays even though the mesh needs no wrapper: the landing squash writes
; Body.position.y, `capture_rest_pose()` reads Body.rotation and the caller writes
; the lean and sway there for BOTH rig kinds. The .glb instance carries NO basis —
; a SKINNED glTF is exported Y-up and placed by its own root node, so the Rx(-90)
; every UNRIGGED part scene applies would lay the hero on his face.

